      "action_copy": "Copy",
      "ag_a2a_d": "Two paired personal agents exchange only start, end, tz, free and ref over their existing SMP session key, signed and replay-protected; titles, attendees and notes cannot leave. A guest books through a one-time /book/{token} HMAC link with no session, no cookie and no script, in all 21 languages, and the .ics invitation exists only after the owner approves.",
      "ag_a2a_t": "Masked A2A negotiation and zero-install booking",
      "ag_agent_d": "Needle 3 is a 33.7 MiB weight file shipped with the repository. It extracts one of five calendar or workspace intents in milliseconds, and a deterministic extractor takes over when the native runtime is missing. Working hours, buffers, blocked periods and keywords per bot decide what counts as free, and every rejected slot keeps a readable reason in the audit log. The calendar is never written until the owner confirms the card.",
      "ag_agent_t": "A 24/7 personal agent that only proposes",
      "ag_flow_cap": "The orchestration state machine in schema v7: eight stages from created to workspace_cleanup, and one terminal branch for failed, cancelled and refused.",
      "ag_grant_d": "A dispatch needs an explicit (origin, target, capability) row in agent_task_grants; the wildcard target must be created on purpose, and every row can be toggled or deleted. Each task lands in SQLite schema v7 with a correlation id, duration, result summary and a stable reason code that orch/replay can reconstruct; the eleven stored statuses run from created to workspace_cleanup, with failed, cancelled and refused as terminal branches.",
      "ag_grant_t": "Grants are denied by default",
      "ag_headline": "One process, a team of agents",
      "ag_note": "Every path above stays on 127.0.0.1. The only outbound calls are to your own model endpoint, a paired agent's SMP queue, or the Mac Node bridge on http://127.0.0.1:18920.",
      "ag_orch_d": "One bot borrows a read-only capability from a sibling — compose a reply, plan a route, mask availability, summarize a workspace or profile the ledger — inside the same studio process. There is no new port, no direct SMP call and no write to another bot's rules. Hops are capped at 3, concurrency at 32, each task times out between 0.5 and 300 seconds, and fan-out is capped at 8 targets.",
      "ag_orch_t": "Process-local multi-agent orchestration",
      "ag_sub": "Each bot keeps its own rules, model key, timezone and calendar cache inside one studio process; a default-deny orchestrator lets one agent borrow what a sibling knows without handing over a single write.",
