      "cap_agent": "agent desk",
      "cap_headline": "An agent workbench, checked against the engine source",
      "cap_sandbox_d": "Every bot gets its own popopx-cli process, its own cli-data directory, its own control port from 5230 to 5299 and its own SQLite files, started and stopped from one screen.",
      "cap_sandbox_t": "Multi-bot sandbox factory",
      "cap_sov_d": "The identity key, the ledger and every message log live in files you own with mode 0600. There is no cloud account to lose and no vendor holding a copy.",
      "cap_sov_t": "Private key and local sovereignty",
      "capabilities_sub": "The blocks people ask about first, each labelled with what is actually built behind the name today. Every claim here was read against the engine repository before it was published.",
      "capm_d": "One OpenAI-compatible call is released, and any vendor that speaks that shape works, including a model you host yourself. What is missing is a registry of providers: today it is one base URL, one model name and one key per bot.",
      "capm_t": "Multiple model providers",
      "capp_d": "Each bot has one editable system prompt, injected as the system message of every model call. The process-local orchestrator can lend a read-only capability to a sibling bot, but one persona per channel or per stage of a conversation is still not implemented.",
      "capp_t": "System prompt and role orchestration",
      "capr_d": "The message ledger, the per-bot log view and the live updates ring are released, and orch/replay returns a whole dispatch chain by correlation id. Stepping a chat conversation back through a run is still not implemented.",
      "capr_t": "Run logs and replay monitoring",
      "capt_d": "Partly implemented. Needle 3 extracts one of five read-only tool intents (calendar availability, propose create/reschedule/cancel, workspace summarize) and never executes a write; a grant table governs which bot may borrow which read-only capability. Model-initiated execution with a per-tool scope check in the dispatcher is still missing.",
      "capt_t": "Tool calling with permission isolation",
      "capv_d": "Defining an agent is released: one record per bot with its own sandbox, token and data directory, plus a cold-backup bundle that carries it to another host. Version management is not: there is no revision history, no publish state and no rollback.",
      "capv_t": "Agent definition and version management",
