      "eco_aria": "POPOPX ecosystem diagram",
      "eco_cap": "Solid lines are the only path wired in code today: the engine drives a local popopx-cli over loopback and reaches SMP with it.",
      "eco_headline": "The POPOPX ecosystem",
      "eco_note": "The four portals share one domain and link to each other, and this page loads nothing from the other three. The dashed edges above, taking a task from POPOPX Chat, calling Service Suite, or dispatching compute to Mac Node, are not implemented in this repository yet. Mac Node does publish a loopback job API; Bot Studio does not call it.",
      "eco_sub": "Four portals on four subdomains of one domain, each a product of its own. This page is the one for the agent workbench.",
      "faq_a1": "Yes. AGPL-3.0 obliges you to share the source of the studio itself when you offer a modified version over a network, including changes to the engine and the plugins. Your bots, rules, reply texts and message data are your content and are not affected. The licence text is in the repository root.",
      "faq_a2": "Routing forwards an enquiry into a support group with a #T ticket id and the bot keeps the original chat reference. Any agent replies with that ticket id, and the engine sends the answer back to the customer only. Every hand is written to the audit log with the actor and the timestamp.",
      "faq_a3": "Export a bundle from the cold-backup screen: the bot is stopped, its cli-data directory, keys and settings are packed, and the bot starts again. Copy the archive to the new host, restore it, and the permanent contact address stays the same because identity lives in those files, not in a vendor account. Restoring is lossless and idempotent: a user already inside cli-data is detected and reused instead of recreated, so the original permanent contact link survives every restart.",
      "faq_a4": "A service account is a rented identity: the provider issues the token, keeps the message graph, sets the rate limits and can end the account. The studio issues the token itself, keeps the ledger on your disk and has no account to close. The trade is that you own the uptime, the backups and the updates.",
      "faq_a5": "The console and the Open API carry an admin token, so an exposed port is the most likely way in. The engine validates the bind address at start-up and refuses a non-loopback host unless you set STUDIO_ALLOW_LAN=1 on purpose. Put Caddy or nginx in front, keep the port closed and add TLS plus your own authentication there.",
      "faq_a6": "The CLI is not committed: the installer fetches the archive for your operating system and architecture from the official releases, verifies the SHA-256 checksum, then unpacks it into the data directory. The repository does ship the Needle 3 weight file (33.7 MiB) so the agent works without a download; it contains no personal data, and nothing about your bots is part of any request.",
