      "plg_hook_t": "Inbound alerts and outbound callbacks",
      "plg_llm_d": "Point it at any compatible base URL, set the model, and the bridge asks only when a rule did not match.",
      "plg_llm_t": "OpenAI-compatible assistant",
      "plg_router_d": "Aggregates alerts, mirrors a direct message into a group and keeps the ticket id attached.",
      "plg_router_t": "Cross-chat and cross-group routing",
      "rm_1_d": "The model would call declared tools, with a scope check enforced in the dispatcher instead of the priority-only ordering that exists now. Needle 3 today extracts the intent but never executes it.",
      "rm_1_t": "Tool calling with per-tool scopes",
      "rm_2_d": "Short-lived grants per bot and per tool with expiry, plus a revoke endpoint for admin and bot tokens that replaces editing .env by hand and restarting.",
      "rm_2_t": "Capability tokens and revocation",
      "rm_3_d": "A revision history for the agent definition, a publish state separate from the runtime state, and rollback to a named revision. Today only the cold-backup bundle moves between hosts.",
      "rm_3_t": "Agent versions and rollback",
      "rm_4_d": "Named vendors with their own keys, quotas and health checks behind the OpenAI-compatible call, instead of one base URL per bot.",
      "rm_4_t": "Model provider registry",
      "rm_5_d": "A persisted event stream you can scrub back through, and a table of who changed what in the console.",
