      "tut_dev_i": "No system service, no sudo: a virtualenv on your laptop with the console on loopback port 8090.",
      "tut_dev_n1": "The engine ships an offline self-test of 10,572 assertions in 26 groups; it needs no network and no real contacts.",
      "tut_dev_n2": "Without STUDIO_ADMIN_TOKEN every admin route answers 401, so an unconfigured checkout cannot be driven by accident.",
      "tut_macos_i": "Registers a launchd agent so the studio comes back after a reboot, using the same installer flags as Linux.",
      "tut_macos_n1": "Every bot is launched through a wrapper script so launchd cannot split the arguments it passes to popopx-cli.",
      "tut_macos_n2": "Backups and the SQLite ledger stay under var/studio, so one archive of that folder is a complete restore point.",
      "tut_quick_i": "Four moves in the console, then the Open API is yours.",
      "tut_quick_n1": "The bot token is minted locally and stored only in the SQLite ledger; rotate it by re-creating the credential in the console.",
      "tut_sub": "Four paths, the same engine: a production Linux box, a Mac you keep running, a development checkout, or the three clicks inside the console.",
      "tut_title": "Install and first run",
      "tut_ubuntu_i": "Installs Python 3.11, creates a system user, writes a systemd unit and pulls popopx-cli for your architecture.",
      "tut_ubuntu_n1": "Open the console through a reverse proxy on your own host: the engine binds 127.0.0.1:8090 and never 0.0.0.0.",
      "tut_ubuntu_n2": "Flags: --check validates the host, --mode native installs in place, --dry-run prints the plan, --uninstall removes the service and keeps your data.",
      "uc_1_d": "Rules answer the common questions, anything unmatched is forwarded into a support group under a #T ticket, and an operator's reply goes back to that one customer.",
      "uc_1_t": "Support desk with tickets",
      "uc_2_d": "A monitoring webhook arrives as a bot message in the right group; the human answer leaves again as a signed callback to your own endpoint, with the ticket id attached.",
      "uc_2_t": "Alert relay for on-call",
      "uc_3_d": "Any script on the same host calls sendMessage with the bot token over loopback, or polls getUpdates, so deploys, queues and cron jobs arrive in chat instead of in a log file.",
      "uc_3_t": "Internal automation",
      "uc_4_d": "The permanent address and its QR code come from key material on your own disk, so moving the data directory to another machine keeps the same reachable identity, and no provider can take the account away.",
      "uc_4_t": "A contact address that never changes",
      "uc_headline": "Four flows that already run",
      "uc_sub": "Each of these is the engine's own behaviour on the day you install it, not a plan: what you can build in the console before the first restart.",
